1-Paragraph Governance Justification (Manager Approval)

Masking is required on [S_cdpdynamics].[CalllogReport] because the dataset 
contains direct patient/member identifiers and PHI-adjacent content (e.g., names,
phone numbers/ANI, emails, addresses, persistent IDs, and free-text transcript/notes fields) that present
a high risk of re-identification and unauthorized disclosure in non-production environments. This approach applies
least-privilege data protection by always masking Critical fields (patient/member PII/PHI) and optionally masking Moderate
workforce/operational identifiers based on a controlled configuration flag, enabling compliance alignment while supporting operational 
testing needs. The solution is automated for new data loads via trigger-based masking and supports consistent application 
across ETL/SSIS ingestion, reducing risk of data leakage and improving audit defensibility.

